    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d485">

                <pb facs="0587" n="575" sameAs="frus:frus1940v03/pg575"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.00111 Armament Control—Military
                    Secrets/3570</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Greek Minister</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Diamantopoulos</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1594</seg>
                </opener>
                <p>The Minister of Greece presents his compliments to His Excellency the Secretary
                    of State and has the honor to enclose herewith two applications<anchor n="62"
                        xml:id="d485-f1"/> for license to export arms, ammunition, or implements <pb
                        facs="0588" n="576" xml:id="pg576"/> of war, for Mr. M. Cavalliotis, agent
                    of the Aegean Trading Company, 154 Nassau Street, New York City, acting for the
                    Greek Government for the supply of war materials, with the request that same be
                    transmitted to the appropriate authorities.</p>
                <p>The Minister of Greece wishes to express his thanks to His Excellency the
                    Secretary of State for his good offices in this matter.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1940-10-11">October 11,
                            1940</date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
